in{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{5} & 2 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{4}{3}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$D=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 15 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix},$\nthen\n\n| $CD=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,.$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |" "If $C=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{5} & 2 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{4}{3}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$$\n\\displaystyle D=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 15 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\nthen\n\n| $CD=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,.$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |"] [:db/cas 17592186299688 :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $A$ and $1$ row in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication: \n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,5=5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -15 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-15=5\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -15 \\\\ -2 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-2=-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -15 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,6=-2\\cdot (-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$AB=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -15 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.$" "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $A$ and $1$ row in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication: \n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,5=5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -15 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-15=5\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -15 \\\\ -2 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-2=-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -15 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,6=-2\\cdot (-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$$\n\\displaystyle AB=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -15 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186299690 :question/problem "If \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}b & a & -b \\\\ -b & a & b \\\\ -b & 0 & -b\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$x=\\begin{bmatrix}-b \\\\ 0 \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix},$\nfind $Ax.$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$Ax=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>" "If \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}b & a & -b \\\\ -b & a & b \\\\ -b & 0 & -b\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$$\n\\displaystyle x=\\begin{bmatrix}-b \\\\ 0 \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\nfind $Ax.$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$Ax=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>"] [:db/cas 17592186299691 :question/problem "If \n$P=\\begin{bmatrix}m & n & -m \\\\ m & -n & -m \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$u=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ p \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},$\nfind $Pu.$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\